 "title": "Amdahl's law",
 "caption": "If 95% of a code runs in parallel, N cores give a speed-up S = 1/(0.05 + 0.95/N). On 100 cores that is 16.8; with infinitely many it can never pass 1/0.05 = 20, because the serial 5% always remains.",
 "alt": "Speed-up against number of cores, rising steeply then flattening towards a dashed limit of 20, with 16.8 at 100 cores marked.",
